**Definition 7.2 (literal traffic and simultaneous backing).** Use
[NLBAII, Definition 65.1][NLBAII]: for reduced $q=n/d$, $d>0$,
$\mathsf b(0)=1$ and

$$
 \ell(q)=2\mathsf b(|n|)+2\mathsf b(d)+3,
 \qquad \ell_{\rm sel}(j)=2\mathsf b(j)+1.
\tag{SC.18}
$$

The exact variable numerical payload on this acquisition is
$k\ell(1)+\sum_{\rm all\ actual\ Reads}\ell(y_i)$, plus one
$\ell_{\rm sel}(j)$ for every Add/Read selector, the growth payloads
in Proposition 7.1, and every actual field/reply/ACK tag and complete
frame/End/local-acknowledgement/Return bit. Construction 4.4 adds its
whole $\ell(q)$ and $\ell(2q)$ and selectors/frames, even at zero.
Charge actual inward/outward copies, design/root/roster ingress,
reports and computed Boundary exports separately. An array export
has its actual count prefix and the sum of literal entry lengths.
No payload formula treats a large rational or address as unit size.

One finite implementation keeps the $2Mk(k+1)$ returned rational
sample slots and their finite phase/call indices while decoding;
derived free/moment arrays may coexist as distinct copies. Infection
can store $Mk(M-k+1)$ rational polynomial coefficients, and a
recurrence solve uses its actual $kM$ by $M$ coefficient system and
augmented right-hand side. These are explicit possible allocations,
not storage minima. Source coefficients/fields, the receiver's
representative and old/new replay vectors, graph and raw table,
genuine references/grants, program/parser/pending buffers, elimination
scratch, output buffers and any archived entrance/kernel coordinates
all require simultaneous backing while live. Distinct copies count
separately; an actual shared allocation counts once; isolated producer
records and later clearing do not erase their backing cost. Keeping
the raw Time tape is optional for prediction and necessary if that
literal tape is to be retained/exported. There is no bound on rational
height, phase, lifetime memory or future growth, and no dimension-only
bit, conditioning, energy or physical installation bound is claimed.

Only the inherited-split coordinate of (SC.11) is proved minimal.
No preliminary old-law scan is necessary, but this does not make the
chosen pulse schedule Read-, Hold-, arithmetic- or total-cost optimal.
Retaining the acquired predictor is already sufficient for ordinary
future service. Retaining a paid entrance archive, accepting a smaller
fixed-topology task, deferring learning, commissioning positive old
links or supplying authentic polarity advice are different resource
contracts. Their favorable coordinates cannot be joined into a
fictional one-run optimum.

